---
import ChickuboInfoLayout from '@/layouts/ChickuboInfoLayout.astro';
---

<ChickuboInfoLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Chickubo handles local farm saves, settings, support messages, and optional purchase services." icon="🔒" updated>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p>Chickubo's core farm progress and preferences are saved on your device. iCloud Save is not connected. Account sign-in, paid checkout, and RevenueCat are not enabled in the current build described by this policy.</p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Who we are and what this policy covers</h2>
    <p>NekoCode develops Chickubo: Cozy Chicken Farm. This policy explains the information handled by the game, optional purchase services when available, and messages you choose to send to support. Contact us at <a href="mailto:support@nekocode.dev?subject=Chickubo%20Privacy">support@nekocode.dev</a> about privacy.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Farm data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>The local save stores chickens and owned breeds, eggs, coins and gems, inventory, housing and upgrades, crop and workshop progress, feed and water supplies, production timers, and timestamps used to calculate offline progress. It also stores tutorial progress, pending game rewards, and preferences such as music and effects volume, Gentle Motion, and in-game notices.</p>
    <p>The game uses this information to load your farm, continue production, remember settings, and prevent duplicate reward delivery. The current build does not upload your farm save to a NekoCode cloud service or synchronize it through iCloud.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Optional accounts and purchases</h2>
    <p>The current build does not enable account sign-in or paid checkout. If a later version makes these features available, purchases will be processed by the platform store. NekoCode does not receive your payment card number.</p>
    <p>Purchase verification requires an account or customer identifier, product identifier, store transaction identifier, receipt or purchase token, purchase state, and reward or delivery records. These records are used to confirm payment, associate a purchase with the correct player, prevent duplicate or fraudulent claims, deliver virtual items, and reconcile refunds or unfinished purchases. The game also keeps local purchase and delivery records when purchases are enabled.</p>
    <p>RevenueCat is planned for optional purchase management and is not active in the current build. When enabled, RevenueCat may process the account or app-user identifier, store receipts and transaction history, purchase and entitlement status, and technical information such as app and operating-system versions and network information. The exact active services and data disclosures will be updated here and in the store listing before those features are enabled.</p>
    <p>Apple and RevenueCat process information under their own policies: <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a>. A purchase account does not itself provide cloud synchronization or recovery of your farm save.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Support messages</h2>
    <p>If you contact us, your email address, message, and any screenshots, device information, or purchase references you choose to include are handled through our email service so we can investigate and reply. Do not send passwords, sign-in tokens, or payment card details. Support messages are separate from the local farm save.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Ads, analytics, and permissions</h2>
    <p>The current game build does not include advertising or third-party analytics services. Core gameplay does not need your location, contacts, camera, or microphone. Opening a support or policy link uses your browser; the destination receives ordinary web-request information under its own policies. Any optional store, account, or verification service needs a network connection when enabled.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Keeping and deleting information</h2>
    <p>Local save data remains within the game's device storage. Removing the app or clearing its data may remove the farm; any device or operating-system backups are controlled by your platform settings. NekoCode cannot remotely erase a local save or promise recovery after it is lost.</p>
    <p>Contact <a href="mailto:support@nekocode.dev?subject=Chickubo%20Privacy%20Request">support@nekocode.dev</a> with a request about support information you have sent us. We may need information to identify your request. If online accounts or purchase services are enabled later, we will explain their retention and account-deletion controls before they are available. Store transaction records may need to be retained for purchase integrity or legal obligations; removing a local save does not delete records held by Apple or another service.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Children and family devices</h2>
    <p>The current game has no online chat or public player profiles. Parents or guardians should supervise optional purchases and any information sent to support. If you believe a child has sent personal information to us that should be removed, contact support with enough detail for us to locate it.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We will update this notice when the game's data practices change and revise the date above. For questions or privacy requests, email <a href="mailto:support@nekocode.dev?subject=Chickubo%20Privacy">support@nekocode.dev</a>.</p>
  </section>
</ChickuboInfoLayout>
